<h2>Tips for the Best Browser Experience</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Use a modern browser:</strong> Chrome, Edge, or Firefox provide the best WebGL support.</li>
  <li><strong>Enable hardware acceleration:</strong> This reduces input lag and improves frame rates.</li>
  <li><strong>Save states wisely:</strong> While convenient, relying solely on save states can diminish the challenge. Try to use the game’s native save system whenever possible.</li>
  <li><strong>Adjust audio latency:</strong> If you notice a delay between button presses and sound, tweak the emulator’s audio buffer in the settings.</li>
  <li><strong>Keyboard vs. controller:</strong> For a more authentic feel, plug in a USB controller. Most modern controllers map directly to the GBA layout.</li>
</ol>

